 995 s wall in the receipt of which 265 s was the release build of every test target, 641 s the nextest Summary (823 tests, 50 slow), 60 s a rebuild before the cargo test invocation and the rest orient_bdd; 823 [[timing]] rows, the first four: lib view::tests::report_produces_cards_and_rejects_unknown 600394 ms, batched_governance_agrees the_batched_path_gives_the_same_answer_as_the_per_item_path 508229 ms, federation f1_a_scaffolded_project_can_make_its_first_commit_at_any_path_shape 407825 ms, land_gate land_refuses_to_push_a_workspace_carrying_a_broken_project 364905 ms. Against the D0474 receipt's cargo test run of the same day (63 binaries, 1246 s wall including its build) that is 1.25x on the receipt's own seconds. MEASURED, before vs after, same 63-binary set of 2026-09-14: cargo test 1246 s wall (per-binary sum 913 s); nextest 723 s at 20 threads, 653 s at 8, 701 s at 4 (test phase alone, 62 binaries); this run's receipt 995 s wall over 68 binaries with 265 s of build in it. The gain is 1.91x at best - UNDER the 2x of D0475's own consequence clause - and the receipt's first timing row says why: view::tests::report_produces_cards_and_rejects_unknown, 347-690 s under contention for a lib whose serial run is 145 s (issue540). The keep-or-supersede judgment on D0475 is deferred to the remeasure after issue540's resolver lands; this record does not make it."; }
