    part nextestIsTheTouchedRunnerImplementGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "be22ccd1-7274-48eb-b412-b13a078e60da"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "d64d319"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification nextestIsTheTouchedRunnerReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "2ed8c661-d264-4e19-889a-2008cf74d931"; :>> title = "Sprint 707 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Three passes (D0172). Correctness: a row is a row only with the (n/N) counter, so the SLOW notice and the post-Summary re-list are not counted (the parser's pair); never_ran applies to each invocation alone, so a nextest list failure names every binary it was given and a cucumber failure names its own; failing is sorted and deduplicated across both. Honesty: the receipt says which runner ran; the cargo-test fallback is labelled and carries no timings rather than invented ones; the measured gain is quoted under D0475's own threshold instead of being rounded to it, and the judgment is deferred to a named remeasure, not made here. Scope: full `keel suite` (no --touched) still runs cargo test - out of D0475's clause, unchanged; `keel land` shares touched::run so it runs under nextest by construction; the count of `cargo test` needles in CI keeps gate-environment-parity's comparison on both workflows."; }
