    verification nextestIsTheTouchedRunnerRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "baed291d-bdbb-4c83-aa13-1eac8bdd11e4"; :>> title = "Sprint 707 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Avoidable issues scanned; findings are tracked items, not prose. Finding one: the number D0475 is judged by is not about the runner - one unit test builds the model eight times over the real tree and is the last test standing in every configuration; issue540, resolver dcReportTestBuildsTheModelOnce, ranked next in the backlog, and the D0475 keep/supersede judgment waits on its remeasure. Finding two: issue539's record and its resolver's DoD said the perf report was on stdout; main.rs already wrote it to stderr and the tests read both streams as one - the records were corrected in this sprint under owner edit, and the lesson is the contract's own: a defect claim names the file:line read. Finding three: the harness = false binaries cannot run under nextest, so the runner is two invocations, and CI mirrors the split by hand (-E 'not (binary(...))'); a workflow that drifts from the manifest would go unnoticed - not tracked as an Issue because custom_harness_tests reads the manifest and its test pins the real trio, so a fourth cucumber binary fails that test before it can drift. Finding four: the cargo test invocation for the cucumber trio recompiled keel-cli for 60 s after nextest had just built it (log lines 1 and 978) - build.rs:47-51 watches ../.git/index, which git status, git ls-files and every self-reading test rewrite, so the provenance script reruns and the crate recompiles after nearly every run; issue541, resolver dcBuildScriptDoesNotWatchTheGitIndex, ranked behind issue540's. Closed in-sprint: the fixture lib's `no tests to run`."; }
